<article class="env-lemma" id="08I8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08I8">Lemma <span data-tag="08I8">36.5.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be an affine morphism of schemes. Then $Rf_* : D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ S)$ reflects isomorphisms. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement means that a morphism $\alpha : E \to F$ of $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is an isomorphism if $Rf_*\alpha $ is an isomorphism. We may check this on cohomology sheaves. In particular, the question is local on $S$. Hence we may assume $S$ and therefore $X$ is affine. In this case the statement is clear from the description of the derived categories $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ S)$ given in Lemma <a href="/tag/06Z0" data-tag="06Z0">36.3.5</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>